CRYPTOGRAPHY ARCHITECTURE

Implement a modular crypto provider abstraction rather than hard-coding algorithms.

Use responsibilities such as:

Post-quantum key establishment (for example ML-KEM where supported)
Digital signatures (for example ML-DSA, with optional support for SLH-DSA)
Symmetric authenticated encryption (for example XChaCha20-Poly1305 or AES-256-GCM)
Password-based key derivation (Argon2id)
Hashing and integrity (BLAKE3 and/or SHA-3 depending on compliance requirements)
HKDF for session key derivation

Design for crypto-agility so algorithms can be upgraded or replaced without changing application logic.

